ist).\n\nThe case payload contains 'tokens' (list of strings) and 'calls' (list of dicts). We need to sort calls by priority: descending score, then start, then call_id (presumably string sort). Then greedily accept if no overlap with already accepted intervals. Overlap: intervals [start, end). Must not overlap. So we need to keep track of occupied intervals.\n\nAfter selection, sort accepted calls by start (ascending). Then apply replacements right to left (descending start) to avoid shifting indices. For each accepted call (in reverse order of start): replace tokens[start:end] with replacement_tokens (list). So we will create a result tokens list.\n\nReturn dict with selected_call_ids (ordered by start) and tokens (the final list).\n\nConstraints: use only standard library, no mutation of input.\n\nLet's write the Python source. We'll define solve(case) that returns dict.\n\nImplementation steps:\n1. Validate required fields? case should have 'tokens' and 'calls'. But according to schema, we don't need to validate, but it's good.\n2. Extract tokens list and calls list.\n3. Rank calls: create list of (score, start, call_id, dict) and sort key = (-score, start, call_id). \n4. Greedy selection: maintain list of selected intervals (start, end). For each candidate in sorted order, check if any selected interval overlaps: if selected_end > candidate_start and selected_start < candidate_end (i.e., intervals intersect). If no overlap, add to selected.\n5. Sort selected by start (ascending).\n6. Create result_tokens = list(tokens) maybe copy.\n7. For each selected call in descending order of start (reversed list), replace slice: result_tokens[start:end] = replacement_tokens.\n8. Return {\"selected_call_ids\": [c['call_id'] for c in selected_sorted], \"tokens\": result_tokens}.\n\nEdge cases: start and end indices should be within bounds? Assume valid.\n\nNote: The output schema requires \"selected_call_ids\" as array of strings, and \"tokens\" as array of strings.\n\nWe ne